WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.140
Toss a coin to your new Witcher.&nbsp;
A major recasting has just rocked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.200
fans of one of Netflix’s biggest&nbsp;
shows. Keep watching to find out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.860
how fans are welcoming the new Geralt&nbsp;
with open arms… or, rather… aren’t.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.760
"The Witcher" has been a firm fan favorite&nbsp;
since first hitting screens in December&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.080
2019. Following hot on the heels of&nbsp;
HBO's "Game of Thrones," the show has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.340
a strong cult following among fantasy-drama&nbsp;
fans. The premiere season was a smash hit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.900
but "The Witcher" Season 2 proved gold for the&nbsp;
streaming platform. Per Variety, it clocked up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.960
"462.5 million hours of view-time," placing it on&nbsp;
Netflix's "most-viewed TV shows of all time list."

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.260
Things have grown from there. "The&nbsp;
Witcher" Season 3 went the extra mile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.280
managing to wrap filming despite&nbsp;
tough times during COVID-19. Lead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.800
actor Henry Cavill wrote on the&nbsp;
show's official Twitter account,

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.880
"What a season this has been! I just want&nbsp;
to thank you all for your determination and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.420
dedication through a tough shoot. Hopefully,&nbsp;
you can all get some well-deserved rest."

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.200
Undoubtedly, one of the show's main&nbsp;
draws is Cavill, who provides both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.500
eye candy and action thrills in&nbsp;
his role of Geralt of Rivia. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.100
when the actor shocked fans by announcing on&nbsp;
his Instagram that he was exiting the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.360
and being replaced by Liam Hemsworth, the&nbsp;
reaction was less than ecstatic. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.780
Cavill fans are hitting the eject button&nbsp;
on "The Witcher" after the recast news.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:14.340
If anyone had any doubt about how "The Witcher"&nbsp;
fans really feel about Henry Cavill as Geralt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.120
they just need a quick glance at his&nbsp;
Instagram feed. Cavill wrote on his page,

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:22.080
"My journey as Geralt of Rivia has been&nbsp;
filled with both monsters and adventures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.620
and alas, I will be laying down my&nbsp;
medallion and my swords for Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:29.520
4. I pass the torch with reverence for&nbsp;
the time spent embodying Geralt and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.120
enthusiasm to see Liam's take on this&nbsp;
most fascinating and nuanced of men."

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.500
Cavill finished by informing Hemsworth that&nbsp;
Geralt, quote, "has such a wonderful depth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.800
to him" and advised the Aussie actor to&nbsp;
dig deep and enjoy playing the character.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.560
Cue the outrage. One fan wrote on Instagram,

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.260
"And just like that, the show crashes and burns."

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.280
Another vowed,

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.180
"I loved your enthusiasm for this character&nbsp;
and how much the series (games and books).&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.360
I am pretty sure I won't watch the&nbsp;
witcher without you being a part of it."

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.820
They shared that they couldn't&nbsp;
imagine the show without Cavill.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.500
One fan went so far as to say,

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.300
"This is the worst day of my life."

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.520
Another said they were (figuratively) hit in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.460
the head by a ton of bricks after&nbsp;
reading his post. They concluded,

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.280
"Shaking head to clear it ... WTF just happened??"

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:12.360
There's no doubt that Cavill did a stellar&nbsp;
job of bringing the lead character of Andrzej&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:17.160
Sapkowski's beloved fantasy novels to life.&nbsp;
His replacement may not be the Man of Steel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.920
but Liam Hemsworth still has&nbsp;
some impressive acting chops.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.120
Some of "The Witcher" fans were kinda,&nbsp;
almost, sort of welcoming to Hemsworth.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.920
A dejected fan wrote to Cavill,

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.080
"I'm sure Liam will bring something to Geralt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.440
but this role was meant for you.... You&nbsp;
brought so much for the show in general.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.680
Geralt will never be the same without&nbsp;
you.... We will miss you so much."

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.740
Ok, perhaps… not really… that welcoming.

